      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the **Guarded Write Journal** works as a transaction mechanism for file operations:\n\n**Key points:**\n\n- Before overwriting any file, the guarded tool executor records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- If an agent run fails (due to hitting a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed before, and deleting newly created files.\n\n- This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, stored only in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\n- The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability.",
